309: % V. DETECTION AND REMEDIATION POLICIES
310: % ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
311: \section{Detection and Remediation Policies}
312: 
313: This section describes the detection signals, evaluation heuristics, and remediation actions for each network subsystem module.
314: 
315: \subsection{CNI Module}
316: 
317: \subsubsection{Detection Signals}
318: The CNI module continuously gathers four categories of signals:
319: \begin{enumerate}
320:   \item \textbf{DaemonSet Health:} Compares \texttt{desiredNumberScheduled} against \texttt{numberReady} on the \texttt{calico-node} DaemonSet. Any mismatch triggers enumeration of unready pods.
321:   \item \textbf{Stuck Workload Pods:} Scans all cluster pods in \texttt{Pending} phase with empty \texttt{podIP}. Pods exceeding the configurable stuck threshold (default: 60\,s) are flagged.
322:   \item \textbf{CNI Event Correlation:} Queries Kubernetes warning events for \texttt{FailedCreatePodSandBox} messages containing CNI/IPAM error signatures.
323:   \item \textbf{IPAM Capacity:} Queries Calico \texttt{IPPool} and \texttt{IPAMBlock} CRDs to detect disabled pools (\texttt{spec.disabled:~true}) and exhausted blocks (100\% utilization).
324: \end{enumerate}
325: 
326: \subsubsection{Evaluation Heuristics}
327: The evaluator applies a strict priority ordering to avoid conflating symptoms with root causes:
328: \begin{enumerate}
329:   \item \emph{Unready calico-node agents} $\to$ \texttt{critical} severity, action: restart agents.
330:   \item \emph{Disabled IPPool with stuck pods} $\to$ \texttt{critical}, action: re-enable pool.
331:   \item \emph{Stuck pods with CNI errors} $\to$ \texttt{critical}, action: evict stuck pods.
332:   \item \emph{IPAM usage $\geq$ threshold} $\to$ \texttt{warning}, no disruptive action (log only).
333: \end{enumerate}
334: 
335: \subsubsection{Remediation Actions}
336: Three targeted remediation branches are executed based on the evaluation:
337: \begin{itemize}
338:   \item \textbf{Restart CNI Agents:} Deletes unready \texttt{calico-node} pods; the DaemonSet controller immediately respawns fresh agents that re-establish BGP routing and veth interfaces.
339:   \item \textbf{Re-enable IPPool:} Patches \texttt{spec.disabled} to \texttt{false} on affected Calico IPPools, unblocking IP allocations.
340:   \item \textbf{Evict Stuck Pods:} Deletes workload pods stranded in \texttt{ContainerCreating} to force rescheduling with clean network namespace initialization.
